OL,3,GNEWSANew school food rules welcomed by
OL,4,Ahead
OL,5,
OL,6,FMany pupils at his school are
OL,7,Funfamiliar with different fruits and
OL,8,Fvegetables, a Telford head teacher has
OL,9,Fsaid as he welcomed new school food
OL,10,Fstandards.
OL,12,FRob Fox, from Donnington Wood CofE
OL,13,FJunior School, said the changes would
OL,14,Fbe particularly important for his
OL,15,Fpupils, about 60% of whom receive free
OL,16,Fschool meals.
OL,18,FNew rules due to be introduced in
OL,19,Fschools from September 2027, would see
OL,20,Fmore fruit and vegetables offered to
OL,21,Fpupils, while deep-fried foods would be
OL,22,Fremoved from menus.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,358,350,200,160,0,100
